From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 13:06:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mkfs: pass the right pointer type to `range_check_64()`

`range_check_64()` takes a `uint64_t *`, but its only caller hands it
`&fssize_db`, which is a `diskaddr_t`:

    mkfs.c:1079:24: error: passing argument 1 of `range_check_64` from
        incompatible pointer type [-Wincompatible-pointer-types]
     1079 |  range_check_64(&fssize_db, "size", 1024LL, ...);
    note: expected `uint64_t *` but argument is of type `diskaddr_t *`

These are the same width but they are not the same type, on illumos as
much as anywhere else: `<sys/int_types.h>` makes `uint64_t` an
`unsigned long` under `_LP64`, while `<sys/types.h>` makes `diskaddr_t`
a `u_longlong_t`. So this is a latent type error in the gate that only
goes unnoticed because nothing here compiles at a warning level that
would object -- not an artefact of building on a foreign host.

Widen the parameter to `diskaddr_t *` rather than casting at the call
site, since `diskaddr_t` is what the one caller has and what a
filesystem size is. The `minimum`/`maximum`/`def_val` parameters stay
`uint64_t`: those are passed by value, so they convert cleanly.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Claude Opus 5)
---
 usr/src/cmd/fs.d/ufs/mkfs/mkfs.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/usr/src/cmd/fs.d/ufs/mkfs/mkfs.c b/usr/src/cmd/fs.d/ufs/mkfs/mkfs.c
index b8acb5fd51..94ed8b734f 100644
--- a/usr/src/cmd/fs.d/ufs/mkfs/mkfs.c
+++ b/usr/src/cmd/fs.d/ufs/mkfs/mkfs.c
@@ -416,7 +416,7 @@ static char checkopt(char *optim);
 static char checkmtb(char *mtbarg);
 static void range_check(long *varp, char *name, long minimum,
     long maximum, long def_val, int user_supplied);
-static void range_check_64(uint64_t *varp, char *name, uint64_t minimum,
+static void range_check_64(diskaddr_t *varp, char *name, uint64_t minimum,
     uint64_t maximum, uint64_t def_val, int user_supplied);
 static daddr32_t alloc(int size, int mode);
 static diskaddr_t get_max_size(int fd);
@@ -5412,7 +5412,7 @@ range_check(long *varp, char *name, long minimum, long maximum,
  * When testing, can compare user_supplied to RC_KEYWORD or RC_POSITIONAL.
  */
 static void
-range_check_64(uint64_t *varp, char *name, uint64_t minimum, uint64_t maximum,
+range_check_64(diskaddr_t *varp, char *name, uint64_t minimum, uint64_t maximum,
     uint64_t def_val, int user_supplied)
 {
 	if ((*varp < minimum) || (*varp > maximum)) {
